          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What sweetener does Thorne whey use?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Thorne sweetens its whey isolate with evaporated cane juice sugar and rebaudioside A, a purified stevia extract, rather than sucralose or acesulfame potassium. That leaves a few grams of sugar per scoop, roughly 2 to 3 g depending on the listing. For most people that is negligible, but strict zero-sugar dieters should know it is there."
          }
